{"context_links":[],"items":{"item-0893e58e32b2a69af2dc01398d40734d":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-0893e58e32b2a69af2dc01398d40734d","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":797,"start":772},{"end":798,"start":797},{"end":896,"start":798},{"end":994,"start":896},{"end":1096,"start":994},{"end":1121,"start":1096},{"end":1122,"start":1121},{"end":1221,"start":1122},{"end":1256,"start":1221},{"end":1257,"start":1256}],"status":"active","text":"## What moves likelihood\n\nUp: a trend that is still moving; a repeat of a failure that has already occurred this period; an\nactive, unmitigated mechanism (corrosion under wet insulation is progressing now); detection by a\nmethod that only catches late-stage damage — a finding detected by ear or smell is further advanced\nthan one detected by UT.\n\nDown: design margin; a measurement inside its acceptance criterion; an item that is out of service\nand not required to be in service.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-f3c2478ce801c2895e35cdd00a236654f31048ceac96b06bcf673e91a778efb6"},"item-11536a0bcb2b7bf6e97c0b9dca193059":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-11536a0bcb2b7bf6e97c0b9dca193059","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"dev_beacon","source_sha256":"58f29e3fd9c927c30c9cbc65a3c5c01961fbce9929c16118bcef9bcf395e088f","spans":[{"end":393,"start":370},{"end":442,"start":393},{"end":493,"start":442},{"end":495,"start":493}],"status":"active","text":"## Quiet instructions\r\nMore reserve marks mean less flutter, not more.\r\nThe chime is possibly late; its state is unknown.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-305cce947981769a80dbb00ce1300b33073b4c4841c6d80c234f077657f54d88"},"item-234cd908251b53a14d0ae0ead654efb1":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-234cd908251b53a14d0ae0ead654efb1","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":210,"start":189},{"end":211,"start":210},{"end":310,"start":211},{"end":411,"start":310},{"end":513,"start":411},{"end":546,"start":513},{"end":547,"start":546},{"end":648,"start":547},{"end":704,"start":648},{"end":705,"start":704},{"end":771,"start":705},{"end":772,"start":771}],"status":"active","text":"## The two questions\n\n**Likelihood** concerns the item itself: given what the inspection found, how likely is it to stop\nperforming its function in the near term. A hairline coating blister on a thick-walled vessel is low\nlikelihood even on a critical vessel. A bearing with a vibration trend that has not plateaued is high\nlikelihood even on a spare pump.\n\n**Impact** concerns what happens if it does fail. This depends mainly on what the equipment does and\nwhat sits behind it, not on the wording of the finding.\n\nThe common error is scoring by how severe the description sounds.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-d0b8aee8afcac7bf9080985724886332c47686c2da8974d031c3b4cb7dd9e49c"},"item-2c18fbbd35efd709730a7708d3fe3bfb":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-2c18fbbd35efd709730a7708d3fe3bfb","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":1918,"start":1894},{"end":1919,"start":1918},{"end":2017,"start":1919},{"end":2117,"start":2017},{"end":2180,"start":2117},{"end":2181,"start":2180},{"end":2284,"start":2181},{"end":2379,"start":2284},{"end":2439,"start":2379},{"end":2440,"start":2439}],"status":"active","text":"## Two recurring errors\n\n**Voted arrangements.** One detector head out of a 2oo3 group is a degradation, not a defeat. The\narrangement still functions, so impact is moderate rather than extreme. It is time-limited, because\nthe group has lost its margin and the next failure defeats it.\n\n**Redundancy is a claim, not a fact.** Check whether the redundant partner is healthy before crediting\nit. If findings exist against both legs of a redundant pair in the same batch, the pair is not\nredundant. Assessing each finding in isolation misses this.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-903ab03e1efb3dc8244d8a5953d10d5ab69d5ae2b40e92b9cbd1963baef59c6f"},"item-37418f5b9cdc097897bb0009f2f627a6":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Equipment: Glass-Carts\r\n","unit_id":"u0014"}],"item_id":"item-37418f5b9cdc097897bb0009f2f627a6","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Glass-Carts"],"source_id":"dev_atlas","source_sha256":"35a95953d27cf67b4385a2c322fe887bb7b928876c2a0cfa5be642c827383818","spans":[{"end":422,"start":407},{"end":446,"start":422},{"end":505,"start":446},{"end":564,"start":505},{"end":566,"start":564}],"status":"active","text":"# Glass-Carts\r\nEquipment: Glass-Carts\r\nMove Glass-Carts only after the chalk square is complete.\r\nMove Glass-Carts only after the chalk square is complete.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-57112f7522051547493c79defa65461933a5eb589329470398087fdf1cdd47ed"},"item-46dbcfc425668085ab5c9e3595f87155":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-46dbcfc425668085ab5c9e3595f87155","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"dev_atlas","source_sha256":"35a95953d27cf67b4385a2c322fe887bb7b928876c2a0cfa5be642c827383818","spans":[{"end":67,"start":0},{"end":69,"start":67}],"status":"active","text":"Atlas festival cue cards; artificial rehearsal instructions only.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-47a63a7ca2ad8dddd6ea0bcef872853a6be8b48771208c296fe86e33c2187328"},"item-5803dbc16922f8df4b1e551907e932c6":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-5803dbc16922f8df4b1e551907e932c6","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"dev_atlas","source_sha256":"35a95953d27cf67b4385a2c322fe887bb7b928876c2a0cfa5be642c827383818","spans":[{"end":577,"start":566},{"end":655,"start":577}],"status":"active","text":"# General\r\nAn uncertain cue stays uncertain; a higher cue number means less brightness.\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-a44a1496a0320cc533ab86385fa3c119c78f0b0afbbd4d339cad9ba8fb8176c8"},"item-736a040fad8dcb7b7dd535fce2301997":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Scope: Brass Desks\r\n","unit_id":"u0012"}],"item_id":"item-736a040fad8dcb7b7dd535fce2301997","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Brass Desks"],"source_id":"dev_quill","source_sha256":"3a004b8eccc41b1be4bceed97313c7bd709513aa3ea4aa73a08000d7b2016094","spans":[{"end":47,"start":0},{"end":84,"start":47},{"end":168,"start":84},{"end":224,"start":168},{"end":305,"start":224},{"end":365,"start":305},{"end":394,"start":365},{"end":473,"start":394},{"end":505,"start":473},{"end":611,"start":505},{"end":623,"start":611},{"end":643,"start":623},{"end":708,"start":643},{"end":773,"start":708}],"status":"active","text":"QUILL ARCHIVE: fictional desk game transcript\r\nQ: Which desk accepts a moon token?\r\nA: The rules in this conversation concern Velvet Desks, also called soft counters.\r\nDo not file a moon token unless its reverse is marked.\r\nException: an unmarked token may rest in the waiting tray, never in the ledger.\r\nThe waiting tray rule qualifies the preceding prohibition.\r\nQ: What does the dial mean?\r\nA: Higher ink stability means lower smudge likelihood, not higher likelihood.\r\nQ: Can a tray be called ready?\r\nA: A ready mark is reported, but another speaker calls readiness unknown; keep that conflict unresolved.\r\nOTHER DESK\r\nScope: Brass Desks\r\nLeave a brass token beside Brass Desks until the arch is drawn.\r\nLeave a brass token beside Brass Desks until the arch is drawn.\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-602cb7f60dbfdc57fcaeea9afa277b9b3612e25a5288155a8168f086454c7903"},"item-7c41fdb258e40eedfad7f9ec57665362":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-7c41fdb258e40eedfad7f9ec57665362","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"dev_atlas","source_sha256":"35a95953d27cf67b4385a2c322fe887bb7b928876c2a0cfa5be642c827383818","spans":[{"end":332,"start":315},{"end":405,"start":332},{"end":407,"start":405}],"status":"active","text":"# Painted pause\r\nDuring a painted pause, keep the ribbon folded even if the bell sounds.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-25837812172d8247a6f6e324160983b918bd3fbbf233c9801418f3c9a3e19952"},"item-7efae9de56d3e90defc3fd0324c03ddf":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-7efae9de56d3e90defc3fd0324c03ddf","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":3186,"start":3167},{"end":3187,"start":3186},{"end":3289,"start":3187},{"end":3390,"start":3289},{"end":3410,"start":3390},{"end":3411,"start":3410},{"end":3512,"start":3411},{"end":3607,"start":3512},{"end":3616,"start":3607},{"end":3617,"start":3616}],"status":"active","text":"## Registry scores\n\n`reliability_score` is 10 = highly reliable, 1 = frequent failures. It runs in the opposite direction\nto likelihood. New starters routinely invert it. `criticality_score` runs in the expected direction,\n10 = most critical.\n\nNeither is sufficient on its own. Criticality is a starting point for impact, reliability a starting\npoint for likelihood; the finding text moves both. A reliable item with a crack in it is still\ncracked.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-80de114a93d0fde97e76abf8b484d1dc0a8b1ecbd05a6410cff802b675da26b8"},"item-7f1e95e85ddf5ec9557518f36f46057b":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-7f1e95e85ddf5ec9557518f36f46057b","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"dev_mosaic","source_sha256":"0852927bd7abe608ce450eb87d6e21a23137fa6394e1e5ea36140d84002c338f","spans":[{"end":298,"start":281},{"end":356,"start":298},{"end":419,"start":356},{"end":488,"start":419},{"end":490,"start":488}],"status":"active","text":"## Scale legend\r\nA higher calmness index implies a lower wobble tendency.\r\nThe dotted-ring exception qualifies the rotation prohibition.\r\nThe observer says the ring may be dotted; this is not confirmation.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-5ea630281af429ce1a949f5b3c3d285eacdb05c56aea609f529686c249757a34"},"item-89d5935a1fdaf9498be846e075d601eb":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-89d5935a1fdaf9498be846e075d601eb","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"dev_mosaic","source_sha256":"0852927bd7abe608ce450eb87d6e21a23137fa6394e1e5ea36140d84002c338f","spans":[{"end":24,"start":0},{"end":78,"start":24},{"end":80,"start":78}],"status":"active","text":"# Mosaic board charter\r\nAll instructions describe an imaginary tile contest.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-1dca982a51cfc901da29c3a55de6492fe2f17c0e9adf10f0ef2ad83c8a485098"},"item-89d94479c6f78495658d8a1c8082c4a3":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-89d94479c6f78495658d8a1c8082c4a3","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":1278,"start":1257},{"end":1279,"start":1278},{"end":1378,"start":1279},{"end":1478,"start":1378},{"end":1581,"start":1478},{"end":1677,"start":1581},{"end":1688,"start":1677},{"end":1689,"start":1688},{"end":1790,"start":1689},{"end":1893,"start":1790},{"end":1894,"start":1893}],"status":"active","text":"## What moves impact\n\nUp: absence of redundancy; Safety Critical Elements, which exist because a major accident scenario\ndepends on them and are judged against that scenario rather than against repair cost; failures that\ndegrade a protection layer rather than causing direct loss; delayed or hidden consequences — loss of\ncorrosion inhibitor has no effect today and a substantial effect in eighteen months; escalation\npotential.\n\nDown: redundancy that is available and capable; items that can be bypassed without loss of function;\natmospheric, non-hydrocarbon, low-energy services; consequences limited to housekeeping or appearance.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-7d092d17031e58771702fd76c77bf2e88ddd3a0fb7f1b07859ceab6c00e0d27a"},"item-8f0a6d182c98f50abd0ad44c190faf5d":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":["folded stars"],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Scope: Paper-Beacons\r\n","unit_id":"u0005"},{"quote":"Aliases: folded stars\r\n","unit_id":"u0006"}],"item_id":"item-8f0a6d182c98f50abd0ad44c190faf5d","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Paper-Beacons"],"source_id":"dev_beacon","source_sha256":"58f29e3fd9c927c30c9cbc65a3c5c01961fbce9929c16118bcef9bcf395e088f","spans":[{"end":93,"start":75},{"end":115,"start":93},{"end":138,"start":115},{"end":190,"start":138},{"end":254,"start":190},{"end":312,"start":254},{"end":314,"start":312},{"end":323,"start":314},{"end":340,"start":323},{"end":363,"start":340},{"end":368,"start":363},{"end":370,"start":368}],"status":"active","text":"## Paper-Beacons\r\nScope: Paper-Beacons\r\nAliases: folded stars\r\n- If a bead is present, do not turn Paper-Beacons.\r\n  - Exception: a silver bead permits one turn after the chime.\r\n  - The silver-bead line qualifies the turn restriction.\r\n\r\n```text\r\n# Not a section\r\nScope: Pretend-Scopes\r\n```\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-9a5462758b0eb92acab3d0a33591d6d02b24c9741100e3fa3bdcc4fe329ea7a1"},"item-8f79eb9758c062995e31d11f44f79069":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-8f79eb9758c062995e31d11f44f79069","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":53,"start":0},{"end":54,"start":53},{"end":156,"start":54},{"end":188,"start":156},{"end":189,"start":188}],"status":"active","text":"# Integrity and Reliability Notes — Bravo Platform\n\nHandover notes from the outgoing Integrity Engineer. Unedited. This is the only written record of how\nfindings are currently triaged.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-7a7b196ed00260532c31fe4c9df78184f9e5a94a9869a90b7f2ecbf0895d0291"},"item-96c4587ca99004a0aaa89521dceeca0c":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Scope: Ochre Tiles\r\n","unit_id":"u0016"}],"item_id":"item-96c4587ca99004a0aaa89521dceeca0c","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Ochre Tiles"],"source_id":"dev_mosaic","source_sha256":"0852927bd7abe608ce450eb87d6e21a23137fa6394e1e5ea36140d84002c338f","spans":[{"end":506,"start":490},{"end":526,"start":506},{"end":579,"start":526},{"end":632,"start":579}],"status":"active","text":"## Ochre Tiles\r\nScope: Ochre Tiles\r\nStack Ochre Tiles only when the paper flag is flat.\r\nStack Ochre Tiles only when the paper flag is flat.\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-791c5768d2ec8dcf3c7614aba5c3bb683833fe7595c5f4060dd80e70026da3c7"},"item-a716a4a9f49df46101a45a8c47f5a164":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-a716a4a9f49df46101a45a8c47f5a164","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":3640,"start":3617},{"end":3641,"start":3640},{"end":3743,"start":3641},{"end":3836,"start":3743},{"end":3934,"start":3836},{"end":3935,"start":3934},{"end":4004,"start":3935},{"end":4005,"start":4004},{"end":4067,"start":4005},{"end":4169,"start":4067},{"end":4219,"start":4169},{"end":4277,"start":4219},{"end":4326,"start":4277}],"status":"active","text":"## Output expectations\n\nMaintenance planning needs two lines: what is wrong, on what, and why it matters — readable without\nopening the inspection record, and not a restatement of the original finding text. Where the\nassessment is uncertain, that should be stated rather than resolved by picking a mid-range score.\n\nRecurring causes of loss of confidence in a triage output, in order:\n\n1. Confidently incorrect scores on safety critical equipment.\n2. Summaries that omit a detail that changes the decision — a measurement, a repeat occurrence, the\n   fact that the standby was already unavailable.\n3. The same finding scored differently on different days.\n4. Uniform mid-range scores across all findings.\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-3fe062a4c361f7cb96d0234c5637b023e732a8653517e03f70b9e4d49fcf19a4"},"item-aa5b0f91b6f00defcd30a741a0643f53":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":["blue counters; sky pieces"],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Equipment: Azure Tiles\r\n","unit_id":"u0005"},{"quote":"Aliases: blue counters; sky pieces\r\n","unit_id":"u0006"}],"item_id":"item-aa5b0f91b6f00defcd30a741a0643f53","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Azure Tiles"],"source_id":"dev_mosaic","source_sha256":"0852927bd7abe608ce450eb87d6e21a23137fa6394e1e5ea36140d84002c338f","spans":[{"end":96,"start":80},{"end":120,"start":96},{"end":156,"start":120},{"end":206,"start":156},{"end":279,"start":206},{"end":281,"start":279}],"status":"active","text":"## Azure Tiles\r\nEquipment: Azure Tiles\r\nAliases: blue counters; sky pieces\r\nWhen a ring is drawn, do not rotate Azure Tiles.\r\nUnless the ring is dotted, the prohibition holds through the next turn.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-0f45a9d8f528814737b4af21ee064e5cd931f180d67246aa9f0d00f4dbc06cd6"},"item-b025c20cd7ea7a355588ba53a8fdd51d":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":["sunset ribbons"],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[{"quote":"Scope: Amber-Kites\r\n","unit_id":"u0004"},{"quote":"Aliases: sunset ribbons\r\n","unit_id":"u0005"}],"item_id":"item-b025c20cd7ea7a355588ba53a8fdd51d","reason":"Source intake","scopes":["Amber-Kites"],"source_id":"dev_atlas","source_sha256":"35a95953d27cf67b4385a2c322fe887bb7b928876c2a0cfa5be642c827383818","spans":[{"end":84,"start":69},{"end":104,"start":84},{"end":129,"start":104},{"end":181,"start":129},{"end":253,"start":181},{"end":313,"start":253},{"end":315,"start":313}],"status":"active","text":"# Amber-Kites\r\nScope: Amber-Kites\r\nAliases: sunset ribbons\r\nDo not raise Amber-Kites while the bell is silent.\r\nIf the bell sounds, raise one ribbon; except during the painted pause.\r\nThe painted pause below qualifies the raising instruction.\r\n\r\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-984d8c76b4f371db1614a79a9fc7e3a1cf448f9898fcbe5db1fe6d68599e16c8"},"item-c9869a6dc646924114c358a37461364b":{"decision_reason":null,"review":null,"review_state":"pending","revision":{"aliases":[],"ancestry":[],"effective_from":null,"effective_until":null,"evidence":[],"item_id":"item-c9869a6dc646924114c358a37461364b","reason":"Source intake","scopes":[],"source_id":"original_domain","source_sha256":"5bdc39e19ca7e885234c391fe24e0ea2e9585af57be456948c2b1506bf8ac066","spans":[{"end":2451,"start":2440},{"end":2452,"start":2451},{"end":2546,"start":2452},{"end":2643,"start":2546},{"end":2741,"start":2643},{"end":2757,"start":2741},{"end":2758,"start":2757},{"end":2774,"start":2758},{"end":2793,"start":2774},{"end":2813,"start":2793},{"end":2844,"start":2813},{"end":2861,"start":2844},{"end":2862,"start":2861},{"end":2964,"start":2862},{"end":3062,"start":2964},{"end":3159,"start":3062},{"end":3166,"start":3159},{"end":3167,"start":3166}],"status":"active","text":"## Urgency\n\nNot an average of likelihood and impact, and not the maximum, though the maximum is closer. A\nlow-likelihood, high-impact finding on an SCE still requires attention this week. A near-certain\nfailure of something inconsequential can wait for the next shutdown. Urgency expresses how soon a\nhuman must act.\n\n- 9–10: today\n- 7–8: this week\n- 5–6: this month\n- 3–4: next planned shutdown\n- 1–2: backlog\n\nTwo conditions override the derived value. Anything that leaves a protection layer impaired without a\nrecorded deviation is immediate, because the installation is out of compliance from the point the\nimpairment is known. The same applies to anything that reduces evacuation capacity below the POB\ncount.\n\n"},"revision_id":"sha256-69aba44a1b18710d2644ca0f193